    11| *   3. Delete rork.json (+ .rorkignore) project config
    12| *   4. Report the EXPO_PUBLIC_RORK_* / EXPO_PUBLIC_TOOLKIT_URL envs to delete
    13| *      from the Render/Expo dashboards (this script never touches secrets)
    14| *   5. Print a proof report of every change
    15| *
    16| * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    17| * WHY THIS IS A SCRIPT AND NOT AN IN-SANDBOX EDIT (read before running):
    18| *
    19| * Inside the Rork-managed sandbox the cloud bundler/preview REQUIRES
    20| * `@rork-ai/toolkit-sdk` + `withRorkMetro`, and Rork's auto-sync RESTORES the
    21| * SDK if it is removed (documented in expo/scripts/verify-expo-sdk.mjs:63-74,
    22| * from the reverted Phase 4e/4f attempt). So removing it there breaks the live
    23| * preview AND gets reverted — it achieves nothing.
    24| *
    25| * This cutover therefore runs on the OWNER'S INDEPENDENT checkout (the GitHub
    26| * repo Render watches), OFF Rork, where withRorkMetro is not needed. It refuses
    27| * to run unless IVX_ALLOW_RORK_CUTOVER=1 is set, so it can never accidentally
    28| * brick the sandbox preview.
    29| *
    30| * Usage (on the independent checkout, NOT in the Rork sandbox):
    31| *   IVX_ALLOW_RORK_CUTOVER=1 node expo/scripts/rork-independence-cutover.mjs
    32| *   IVX_ALLOW_RORK_CUTOVER=1 node expo/scripts/rork-independence-cutover.mjs --dry-run
    33| *
    34| * After running: `bun install` in expo/ (refreshes the lockfile without the SDK),
    35| * `bunx expo start` to verify the app launches on the plain Metro config, then
    36| * commit + push → Render auto-deploy.
    37| */
